Let me add that if (when!) the typeahead buffer bug gets fixed, there is
another enhancement that should go in at the same time -- that is, some
way to avoid endless --more-- prompts.  I have hit many situations where
I just kept the space bar pressed down for >10 seconds, winding up with
a ton of flashing --more-- prompts followed by a ton of flashing
"unknown command" messages.  The ultimate must have been when I was
trapped behind a red dragon and an orange dragon in a corridor:

The blast of sleep gas hits the red dragon.
The blast of sleep gas hits you.
The blast of sleep gas hits the red dragon.
The blast of sleep gas whizzes by you.
<<repeat last 2 lines 100 times>>
The blast of sleep gas hits you.
<<repeat a thousand or so more times>>
You can move again.
unknown command ' '
<<repeat another thousand more times>>

